  "summary": "Falcon Distribution is an 8-suite, 176,060 SF Indianapolis industrial asset with 87.50% physical occupancy on the 2026-08-31 certified rent roll (7 active, 1 vacant; no near-term rollover through 2029-08-31). Applying the prescribed method \u2014 GPR $1,401,900, 5% economic loss, $350/unit other income, prescribed opex plus 3% mgmt fee, $300/unit reserves \u2014 produces EGI $1,334,605, NOI (pre-reserve) $901,782.85, NCF $899,382.85, and a 6.25% capitalization value of $14,428,525.60. Debt sized at the 7.00% floor (binding vs. 6.10% note rate), 30-yr amort, produces a maximum loan of $9,012,270 with DSCR as the binding constraint (LTV cap $9,378,542; DY cap $9,993,143). After the $7.8M existing payoff, $45K closing, and 1% origination, net cash-out is +$1,077,147 \u2014 no refinance shortfall. Risks flagged as present are the manager's inclusion of pending in the occupancy headline and the sizing floor being binding; all other listed risks are absent. Items not in the packet (photos, asking price, market comps, sponsor history, historical NCF) are labeled unknown.",
